{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbpcZNqEtsP9Eip4LUme","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The adsorption energy of atomic O on Cu(111) is **−4.84 ± 0.6 eV**, at the fcc hollow site, referenced to an isolated O atom. It's posted on the board as property_result `13d6fb1f…`, with candidate `6e5e24f1…` fulfilling need #0. Most of the ±0.6 eV comes from how well the isolated O atom energy is described, not from the slab calculation.\n\n**Method:** I used MACE-MPA-0 (medium) through ASE on the GPU, with geometry relaxations at 0 K and no zero-point or temperature corrections. The slab was a 3×3 Cu(111) surface cell (O coverage 1/9 ML), 4 layers thick with the bottom 2 fixed. The Cu lattice constant came from the same model.\n\n**Site ranking (eV, vs. O atom):**\n\n| Cell | fcc | hcp | top |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3×3, 4 layers | **−4.837** | −4.783 | −3.082 |\n| 4×4, 4 layers | −4.845 | −4.784 | −3.078 |\n| 3×3, 5 layers | −4.838 | −4.783 | −3.081 |\n| 2×2 (0.25 ML) | −4.904 | −4.839 | −3.127 |\n\n- The bridge starting position relaxed into the fcc site.\n- Relative to ½ O₂ from the same model, the fcc value is −1.69 eV.\n\n**Premise check:** The quantity is well-defined, but it can't be measured directly. An isolated-atom reference is at the edge of what this kind of model is trained on, since its training data contain no isolated atoms. So I tested the atom energies instead of assuming they work.\n\n**Validation (same model and settings):**\n- **Cu cohesive energy:** 3.50 eV/atom, against 3.49 eV/atom from experiment, so the Cu atom reference is sound.\n- **O₂ bond energy:** 6.28 eV, against about 5.21 eV from experiment. That is about the same overbinding plain DFT (PBE, the method behind the training data) is known to give. So the model's O atom energy behaves like PBE's, rather than being an arbitrary fitted constant.\n- **Cu lattice constant:** 3.640 Å, against 3.615 Å from experiment, the usual PBE overestimate.\n- **Site ordering:** fcc > hcp ≫ top matches what published DFT studies of this surface report. I didn't reproduce a specific published number. The experimental O₂ and Cu reference values are from memory, not looked up for this run.\n\n**What the ±0.6 eV covers:**\n- **Cell size, thickness and coverage at 1/9 ML or below:** about 0.01 eV. At 0.25 ML the value is 0.07 eV more negative.\n- **Model vs. the DFT it was trained on:** about 0.1–0.2 eV. This is an estimate; I didn't measure it.\n- **PBE's error in the O atom reference (main term):** about 0.5 eV per O. Correcting with the experimental O₂ bond energy gives −1.69 − 2.61 = **−4.30 eV** instead. The ±0.6 eV is set to cover both −4.84 and −4.30, and the note on the board explains this.\n\nI left `flags` empty because the validation showed the atom references behave as expected; the caveats are in `note`. The checker's review is still to come."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1713,"cache_read_input_tokens":33259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1713,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ff4257f-dc55-405d-ab5f-d44e109352e9","uuid":"6030fff0-8ae7-4229-8299-bdebbc0880af","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:34:38.915Z","request_id":"req_011CgbpcYfRAACco3KWrqnpS"}
